{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KummerDilogHalf","lean:module:QOU.Knot.IdealTetLawOfSines","lean:module:QOU.Knot.RivinConcavity"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.kummer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.kummer","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L274-L305","doc":"**KUMMER'S IDENTITY, general `z`.**\n\nFor every `z` with `Im z > 0`,\n\n    `BlochWigner_lob z = Im cLiTwoExt z + log‖z‖ · arg(1 − z)`\n\n— the corpus's angle-built Bloch–Wigner function **is** the dilogarithm one.\n\nProof: along the ray through `z`, the defect has vanishing derivative\n(`hasDerivAt_defect_zero`, which is the law of sines in disguise), so it is\nconstant; at `r = 1` it vanishes by `KummerDilogHalf.kummer_unit_circle`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:kummer-bloch-wigner-identity","label":"thm:kummer-bloch-wigner-identity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/kummer-bloch-wigner-identity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_defect_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_defect_zero","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L248-L272","doc":"**The Kummer defect is constant along every ray**, because both sides move at\n`−log r · θ₂′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.eq_of_hasDerivAt_zero_Ioi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.eq_of_hasDerivAt_zero_Ioi","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L235-L246","doc":"Constancy from a vanishing derivative on `Ioi`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.arg_one_sub_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.arg_one_sub_eq","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L230-L233","doc":"`arg(1 − z) = −θ₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_lobSide","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_lobSide","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L179-L226","doc":"`d/dr (Λ(θ₁) + Λ(θ₂) + Λ(θ₃)) = −log r · θ₂′` — the law of sines is what\nturns the two `Λ′` terms into `−log r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_im_cLiTwoExt_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_im_cLiTwoExt_ray","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L149-L177","doc":"`d/dr Im cLiTwoExt(r e^{iφ}) = θ₂ / r`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₃_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₃_eq","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L140-L145","doc":"`θ₃ = π − φ − θ₂` along the ray: the angle sum with `θ₁ = φ` frozen. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₃_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₃_mem","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L136-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₂_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₂_mem","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L132-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_tetAngle₂_ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.hasDerivAt_tetAngle₂_ray","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L94-L126","doc":"The derivative of `θ₂` along the ray.  Its **value** is never used — only\nthat it exists, and that both sides of Kummer move at `−log r` times it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.one_sub_mem_slit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.one_sub_mem_slit","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L87-L92","doc":"`1 − z` is off the slit whenever `Im z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₂_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.tetAngle₂_eq","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L74-L85","doc":"`θ₂ = −arg(1−z) = −Im log(1−z)` on the upper half plane. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_arg","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L66-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_im","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L58-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray_norm","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L53-L56","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.KummerRadial.ray","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KummerRadial.lean#L48-L49","doc":"The ray through `e^{iφ}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}